      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Given your stage 3 kidney disease, **you must not take any potassium supplements without explicit approval from your nephrologist**, as your kidneys may already struggle to regulate potassium levels, leading to dangerous hyperkalemia. Muscle cramps and fatigue in your condition can stem from various electrolyte imbalances or other factors like uremia, so a blood test is essential for accurate diagnosis before treatment. Never self-medicate with supplements when your kidney function requires strict dietary and medication monitoring to avoid life-threatening complications.",
